sequenceDiagram
    participant Client
    participant S3Gateway as API Gateway (S3Gateway)
    participant FileController
    participant FileService
    participant S3Repository
    participant AWSS3 as AWS S3

    %% Step 1: Client requests pre-signed delete URL
    Client->>S3Gateway: POST /s3/presigned/delete<br/>with file key
    S3Gateway->>FileController: Forward request
    FileController->>FileService: Request pre-signed delete URL
    FileService->>S3Repository: Generate pre-signed delete URL
    S3Repository->>AWSS3: Request pre-signed URL (DELETE method)
    AWSS3-->>S3Repository: Return pre-signed URL
    S3Repository-->>FileService: Return URL
    FileService-->>FileController: Return URL
    FileController-->>S3Gateway: Send pre-signed URL
    S3Gateway-->>Client: 200 OK — Pre-signed delete URL returned

    %% Step 2: Client deletes file directly
    Client->>AWSS3: DELETE file using pre-signed URL
    AWSS3-->>Client: 204 No Content — File deleted successfully

    %% Step 3: (Optional) Notify backend of deletion completion
    Client->>S3Gateway: POST /s3/notifyDeleteComplete<br/>with file key
    S3Gateway->>FileController: Forward notification
    FileController->>FileService: Update logs / publish "file_deleted" event